# baseURI: https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/
#
# starshacl's own self-declared SHACL 1.2 conformance statement, per SHACL
# 1.2 Profiling S3 ("Profiles of SHACL", https://www.w3.org/TR/shacl12-profiling/)
# - which of the spec family's named feature profiles this library implements,
# expressed with the same dx-prof (`prof:`, https://www.w3.org/TR/dx-prof/)
# vocabulary S3 itself uses, rather than only in the prose gap matrix
# (docs/shacl12-gap-matrix.md).
#
# This is a self-declaration, not a third-party certification - and both
# this library and every SHACL 1.2 document it profiles are still W3C
# Working Drafts as of dcterms:modified below, so treat it as a dated
# snapshot. docs/shacl12-gap-matrix.md is the authoritative, continuously
# updated, per-predicate source of truth; re-derive this file from it
# (don't hand-drift the two) whenever conformance status materially
# changes.
#
# Declares the Profiling Profile itself
# (http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl/profile/profiling), revisited 2026-10-09:
# this document's S2 packaging conventions (sh:ShapesGraph membership via
# rdfs:member/rdfs:isDefinedBy/owl:imports, extract_shapes_graph()) and
# S5.5's sh:conformsTo inference rule (derive_conforms_to(), now also
# merged automatically into validate()'s own report whenever both graph
# IRIs are resolved) are both built - the earlier judgment call to leave
# this undeclared no longer reflects how much of S2/S5.5 is real,
# exercised behavior rather than inert pass-through metadata.
#
# Deliberately does NOT declare the UI Profile
# (http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl/profile/ui) - asserted below as an explicit
# conformance:doesNotConformTo triple (2026-10-09), not just this prose,
# so a caller querying the graph sees the exclusion as real data rather
# than needing to read this file's own header comment: shui: annotations
# pass through inertly (confirmed), but the profile's own
# widget-selection algorithm (shui:WidgetScore/shui:WidgetAcceptMatcher)
# is unimplemented - see docs/shacl12-gap-matrix.md's "Not Covered /
# Deferred" table. conformance:doesNotConformTo is this project's own
# minted term (starlayer/conformance.py's own docstring explains why - no
# standard "does not conform" predicate exists in dx-prof/Dublin Core to
# reuse instead).
#
# Not declared at all (no known IRI in the published draft, and not
# tracked by the gap matrix): the community-managed CD1/Pretty
# Print/OWL Consistent/SHACL 1.0 profiles mentioned in S3.
#
# Subject IRI and seeAlso fixed 2026-10-14: both still named the
# pre-merge "packages/shacl" path (a known, previously-flagged-but-undone
# drift bug - see starlayer/starontology/__init__.py's own comment on
# _resource_iri(), written before this fix and updated alongside it) -
# this repo has had no packages/shacl directory since the three-package
# merge into packages/starlayer. Now packages/starlayer/starlayer/shacl,
# matching starlayer/assets/starlayer-conformance.ttl's own already-
# correct convention for this exact package.

@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix conformance: <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/ns/conformance#> .

<https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/tree/main/packages/starlayer/starlayer/shacl>
    rdfs:label "starshacl" ;
    rdfs:comment "pySHACL-based SHACL validation and rule execution with RDF 1.2 / triple-term support, part of the StarLayer stack."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Not claimed: the UI Profile (widget-selection algorithm unimplemented - see this file's own header comment for the full reasoning)."@en ;
    dcterms:modified "2026-10-14"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/blob/main/packages/starlayer/docs/shacl/shacl12-gap-matrix.md> ;
    dcterms:conformsTo
        <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl/profile/core> ,
        <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl/profile/sparql> ,
        <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl/profile/node-expr> ,
        <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl/profile/rules> ,
        <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl/profile/profiling> ;
    conformance:doesNotConformTo <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl/profile/ui> .
